  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone, through its indication for Chronic Beryllium Disease and Erythema Multiforme, is linked to Methylprednisolone and Hydrocortisone Acetate, all of which are known to induce Humoral Hypercalcemia Of Malignancy. This relationship is supported by the shared pathway of drug-induced hypercalcemia, where corticosteroids like these elevate calcium levels by suppressing the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system and reducing calcium reabsorption in the kidneys. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may act through a similar mechanism, potentially by modulating calcium homeostasis, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of corticosteroids in triggering hypercalcemia, emphasizing the importance of understanding their pharmacological effects in clinical contexts."
